# Tips vs When — no schedule duplication

## Core rule

> **If it belongs in WHEN, do not repeat it in Good to know.**

Parents already see dates, hours, Through, and festival window labels in the When block. Tips should add *other* useful info (tickets, parking, what to bring, crowd notes) — not restate the schedule.

## Put in WHEN (not tips)

- Opening / next open / Open TODAY / Tomorrow…
- Operating hours
- Recurrence (Daily, Weekends, Sat–Sun)
- Through [close date]
- Multi-day window lines (e.g. `During Labor Day weekend · Sep 5–7`)
- Date spans already shown as `Sep 19–20`

## Keep in Good to know

- Ticket / registration links and policies
- Parking, strollers, crowds, what to bring
- Variable hours caveat (“hours vary — check the farm calendar”) when WHEN only shows a representative open-day time
- Editorial notes that are *not* the schedule itself

## Avoid

| Avoid in tips | Prefer |
| --- | --- |
| Sat–Sun Sep 19–20 · 11am–5pm on Grant Avenue | (WHEN shows range + Sat–Sun · hours) |
| Open September 17–November 2, 7 days a week | (WHEN shows Opens / Daily · hours / Through Nov 2) |
| Labor Day weekend Sep 5–7 only | (WHEN shows During Labor Day weekend · Sep 5–7) |
| Sat Sep 26 · 11am–4pm at Presidio Main Parade Lawn | (WHEN shows the date + hours; tip can say Free admission / RSVP / parking) |

